    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Born in Guangdong, Wan Zhu fled to Hong Kong during the Cultural Revolution and became curator for the Museum of Chinese Historical Relics in Wanchai. A distinguished silver-haired gweilo visitor won her trust and, one night, Embraced her under pretext of authenticating a jade artifact &mdash; then secretly Blood Bound her, in violation of @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} law. Wan Zhu now serves as Oliver Thrace's eye on the Kuei-jin community, having learned enough of Cathayan society to briefly pass among them. Torn between resentment of her sire's abuse and the compulsion of the Blood Bond, she quietly plots to free herself.</p><h2>Image</h2><p>An elegant woman in her 30s who dresses in traditional Chinese clothing at Thrace's command, carrying herself with a practiced meekness that conceals an assertive nature.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Obey Thrace outwardly while nursing resentment; look for any opportunity to break the Blood Bond, even if it means throwing herself on the mercy of the Kuei-jin.</p><h2>Haven</h2><p>Resides in the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} Chantry with her sire.</p>",
    "notes": "Disciplines (as printed): Auspex 3, Fortitude 2, Thaumaturgy 2 (Blood 2, Elemental Control 1, Movement of Mind 1). Rituals: Defense of the Sacred Haven, Communicate with Kindred Sire. Thrace has deliberately withheld Dominate from her. Sire: Oliver Thrace (Blood Bound to him).",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
